.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-DELETE-KEY 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key \- schedule an encryption key for deletion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm delete-key
.BR \-\-key\-id | \-k
.I KEY_ID
[\fB\-\-pending\-window\-days\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIDAYS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Schedules a key for permanent deletion after a grace period,
.I DAYS
days from now (default
.IR 7 ).
The key is not deleted immediately. Its status becomes
.BR PENDING_DELETION :
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-decrypt (1)
keeps working for the whole grace period, giving time to decrypt or
migrate everything that was encrypted under the key, but
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt (1)
is blocked right away, the same as after
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1).
Once the grace period elapses, the server's background purge sweep
deletes the key and its material for good; there is no undo.
.PP
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1)
shows a
.B status
of
.B PENDING_DELETION
and a
.B deletionDate
field for any key that has been scheduled for deletion, so pending
deletions stay visible until they take effect.
.PP
Calling
.B delete-key
again on the same key reschedules it, replacing the previous deletion
date with a new one computed from
.B \-\-pending\-window\-days
at the time of the call.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key\-id " " \fIKEY_ID\fR
ID of the key to schedule for deletion, as returned by the
.B name
field of
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1).
Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-pending\-window\-days " " \fIDAYS\fR
Number of days to wait before the key is permanently deleted. Defaults
to \fI7\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The key was scheduled for deletion; its ERN, name and computed
deletion date are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request (e.g. unknown key ID).
.SH EXAMPLES
Schedule a key for deletion using the default 7-day grace period:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm delete-key \e
    --key-id 3f1c2b7a-...
.fi
.RE
Schedule a key for deletion in 30 days instead:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm delete-key \e
    --key-id 3f1c2b7a-... --pending-window-days 30
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-decrypt (1)
